add('ex', 13, 1, 'Matthew Henry', 'Êxodo 13:1 — Matthew Henry: Care is here taken to perpetuate the remembrance,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ I. Of the preservation of Israel s firstborn, when the firstborn of the Egyptians were slain. In...', 'teologico', 'resumo');
add('ex', 13, 11, 'Matthew Henry', 'Here we have,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nI. Further directions concerning the dedicating of their firstborn to God. 1. The firstlings of their cattle were to be dedicated to God, as part of their possessions. Those of clean beasts - calves, lambs, and kids - if males, were to be sacrificed, Exo 22:30; Num 18:17, Num 18:18. Those of unclean beasts, as colts, were to be redeemed with a lamb, or knocked on the head. For whatsoever is unclean (as we all are by nature), if it be not redeemed, will be destroyed, Exo 13:11, E...', 'teologico', 'resumo');
