add('js', 4, 1, 'Matthew Henry', 'We may well imagine how busy Joshua and all the men of war were while they were passing over Jordan, when besides their own marching into an enemy\'s country, and in the face of the enemy, which could not but occasion them many thoughts of hear, they had their wives, and children, and families, their cattle, and tents, and all their effects, bag and baggage, to convey by this strange and untrodden path, which we must suppose either very muddy or very stony, troublesome to the weak and frightfu...', 'teologico', 'resumo');
