add('jz', 8, 1, 'Matthew Henry', 'Juízes 8:1 — Matthew Henry: No sooner were the Midianites, the common enemy, subdued, than, through the violence of some hot spirits, the children of Israel were ready to quarrel...', 'teologico', 'resumo');
add('jz', 8, 4, 'Matthew Henry', 'Juízes 8:4 — Matthew Henry: In these verses we have,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ I. Gideon, as a valiant general, pursuing the remaining Midianites, and bravely following his blow. A very great slaughter was...', 'teologico', 'resumo');
add('jz', 8, 18, 'Matthew Henry', 'Judgment began at the house of God, in the just correction of the men of Succoth and Penuel, who were Israelites, but it did not end there. The kings of Midian, when they had served to demonstrate Gideon\'s victories, and grace his triumphs, must now be reckoned with. 1. They are indicted for the murder of Gideon\'s brethren some time ago at Mount Tabor. When the children of Israel, for fear of the Midianites, made themselves dens in the mountains (Jdg 6:2), those young men, it is likely, took ...', 'teologico', 'resumo');
add('jz', 8, 22, 'Matthew Henry', 'Juízes 8:22 — Matthew Henry: Here is, I. Gideon s laudable modesty, after his great victory, in refusing the government which the people offered him. 1. It was honest in...', 'teologico', 'resumo');
add('jz', 8, 29, 'Matthew Henry', 'Juízes 8:29 — Matthew Henry: We have here the conclusion of the story of Gideon. 1. He lived privately, Jdg 8:29. He was not puffed up with his great honours,...', 'teologico', 'resumo');
