add('sl', 6, 1, 'Matthew Henry', 'These verses speak the language of a heart truly humbled under humbling providences, of a broken and contrite spirit under great afflictions, sent on purpose to awaken conscience and mortify corruption. Those heap up wrath who cry not when God binds them; but those are getting ready for mercy who, under God\'s rebukes, sow in tears, as David does here. Let us observe here,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nI. The representation he makes to God of his grievances. He pours out his complaint before him. Whither else should a chil...', 'teologico', 'resumo');
