add('sl', 14, 1, 'Matthew Henry', 'Salmos 14:1 — Matthew Henry: If we apply our hearts as Solomon did (Ecc 7:25) to search out the wickedness of folly, even of foolishness and madness, these verses will...', 'teologico', 'resumo');
add('sl', 14, 4, 'Matthew Henry', 'In these verses the psalmist endeavours,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nI. To convince sinners of the evil and danger of the way they are in, how secure soever they are in that way. Three things he shows them, which, it may be, they are not very willing to see - their wickedness, their folly, and their danger, while they are apt to believe themselves very wise, and good, and safe. See here,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n1. Their wickedness. This is described in four instances: - (1.) They are themselves workers of iniquity; they design it, they practis...', 'teologico', 'resumo');
add('sl', 15, 1, 'Tomás de Aquino', 'Quem habitará no teu tabernáculo? O acesso à presença de Deus requer integridade.', 'aplicacao', 'resumo');
