add('sl', 119, 140, 'Matthew Henry', 'Salmos 119:140 — Matthew Henry: Here is, 1. David s great affection for the word of Deus: Thy servant loves it. Every good man, being a servant of Deus, loves...', 'teologico', 'resumo');
add('sl', 119, 141, 'Matthew Henry', 'Here is, 1. David pious and yet poor. He was a man after God\'s own heart, one whom the King of kings did delight to honour, and yet small and despised in his own account and in the account of many others. Men\'s excellency cannot always secure them from contempt; nay, it often exposes them to the scorn of others and always makes them low in their own eyes. God has chosen the foolish things of the world, and it has been the common lot of his people to be a despised people. 2. David poor and yet...', 'teologico', 'resumo');
