add('sl', 119, 156, 'Matthew Henry', 'Salmos 119:156 — Matthew Henry: Here, 1. David admires Deus s grace: Great are thy tender mercies, O Lord! The goodness of Deus s nature, as it is his glory,...', 'teologico', 'resumo');
add('sl', 119, 157, 'Matthew Henry', 'Salmos 119:157 — Matthew Henry: Here is, 1. David surrounded with difficulties and dangers: Many are my persecutors and my enemies. When Saul the king was his persecutor and enemy...', 'teologico', 'resumo');
add('sl', 119, 158, 'Matthew Henry', 'Here is, 1. David\'s sorrow for the wickedness of the wicked. Though he conversed much at home, yet sometimes he looked abroad, and could not but see the wicked walking on every side. He beheld the transgressors, those whose sins were open before all men, and it grieved him to see them dishonour God, serve Satan, debauch the world, and ruin their own souls, to see the transgressors so numerous, so daring, so very impudent, and so industrious to draw unstable souls into their snares. All this c...', 'teologico', 'resumo');
