add('jr', 10, 17, 'Matthew Henry', 'Jeremias 10:17 — Matthew Henry: In these verses,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ I. The prophet threatens, in Deus s name, the approaching ruin of Judah and Jerusalem, Jer 10:17, Jer 10:18. The Jews that...', 'teologico', 'resumo');
add('jr', 11, 1, 'Matthew Henry', 'The prophet here, as prosecutor in God\'s name, draws up an indictment against the Jews for wilful disobedience to the commands of their rightful Sovereign. For the more solemn management of this charge,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nI. He produces the commission he had to draw up the charge against them. He did not take pleasure in accusing the children of his people, but God commanded him to speak it to the men of Judah, Jer 11:1, Jer 11:2. In the original it is plural: Speak you this. For what he said to Jeremiah was th...', 'teologico', 'resumo');
